cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Speak Before the Reveal: cheat sheet skill and worked examples"
message: "If you use this skill or the cheat sheets, please cite both this repository and the method paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jurblum
    given-names: Marc
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2208-7042"
    affiliation: "The University of Melbourne"
abstract: >-
  An LLM skill that interviews a clinician and builds a printable prompt card
  for use with an AI scribe, together with two worked examples (psychiatry and
  general medicine). The card prompts the clinician to speak their clinical
  reasoning aloud before the scribe generates its note, so that the reasoning
  is authored rather than edited and the record carries the clinician's
  thinking rather than a plausible reconstruction of it.
keywords:
  - AI scribe
  - ambient documentation
  - clinical reasoning
  - deskilling
  - cognitive offloading
  - clinical documentation
  - psychiatry
  - health informatics
license: CC-BY-4.0
